A dilation with a scale factor \( k \) transforms a point \((x, y)\) into \((kx, ky)\). In matrix form, this transformation can be represented as:

\[
\begin{bmatrix}
x' \\
y'
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
