Note that triangles $ABP,$ $BCP,$ and $CDP$ have the same base and height, so their areas are equal.  Let $K = [ABP] = [BCP] = [CDP].$

We have that
\[[APC] = \frac{1}{2} ac \sin \angle APC = \frac{3}{10} ac,\]so $K = \frac{1}{2} [APC] = \frac{3}{20} ac.$

